(module harness-api-description)

;;; This is the machine-readable source of truth for the public Gatekeeper
;;; surface. The route root returns it when JSON is requested, and Gatekeeper's
;;; catalog reads the same document through gk_describe.
(defn harness-api-description-json [] (-> (slice u8))
  "{\"name\":\"coil-agent-harness\",\"version\":1,\"summary\":\"Create and observe durable agent runs, invoke harness tools, or execute queued runs with an external worker.\",\"primary_use\":{\"summary\":\"Declare a named project, write a reusable Markdown workflow, then run that workflow against the project in an isolated Git worktree.\",\"steps\":[\"Declare the checkout in projects.json and confirm it with harness projects.\",\"Create factory.json plus shared context Markdown and ordered worker Markdown files.\",\"Run harness factory run with the workflow folder and project name.\",\"Keep the printed workspace, branch, journal, and snapshotted definition; inspect progress and review the committed branch.\"],\"nouns\":{\"project\":\"A stable name for an existing checkout.\",\"workflow\":\"Reusable factory metadata and Markdown worker instructions.\",\"run\":\"One isolated execution of a workflow on a project.\"}},\"discovery\":{\"text\":\"GET /agents\",\"json\":\"GET /agents?format=json\"},\"conventions\":{\"content_type\":\"application/json for request and buffered response bodies\",\"mutation_version\":1,\"idempotency\":\"Reuse the same command_id when retrying a mutation that accepts command_id.\",\"errors\":{\"shape\":{\"error\":\"machine_readable_code\",\"message\":\"human-readable explanation\"},\"common_statuses\":[400,404,409,500,501,503]},\"events\":{\"poll_cursor\":\"Pass ?after=<sequence>; next_cursor is the durable resume position.\",\"sse_cursor\":\"Pass ?after=<sequence> or Last-Event-ID. Each event has an id; the stream closes when the run is terminal.\"}},\"quickstarts\":{\"list_tools\":{\"method\":\"GET\",\"methods\":[\"GET\"],\"path\":\"/agents/v1/tools\"},\"call_tool\":{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/agents/v1/tools/call\",\"body\":{\"name\":\"echo\",\"arguments\":{\"text\":\"hello\"}}},\"create_run\":{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/agents/v1/runs\",\"body\":{\"version\":1,\"command_id\":\"create-unique-id\",\"run_id\":\"run-unique-id\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"prompt\":\"Inspect the workspace and report what you find.\"}},\"create_worker_run\":{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/agents/v1/runs\",\"body\":{\"version\":1,\"command_id\":\"create-worker-unique-id\",\"run_id\":\"worker-run-unique-id\",\"provider\":\"external\",\"model\":\"agent\",\"prompt\":\"Do the assigned work.\",\"execution_target\":\"worker\"}},\"inspect_run\":{\"method\":\"GET\",\"methods\":[\"GET\"],\"path\":\"/agents/v1/runs/{run_id}\"},\"poll_events\":{\"method\":\"GET\",\"methods\":[\"GET\"],\"path\":\"/agents/v1/runs/{run_id}/events?after=0\"},\"stream_events\":{\"method\":\"GET\",\"methods\":[\"GET\"],\"path\":\"/agents/v1/runs/{run_id}/events/stream?after=0\",\"response\":\"text/event-stream\"}},\"endpoints\":[{\"method\":\"GET\",\"methods\":[\"GET\"],\"path\":\"/v1/tools\",\"purpose\":\"List available tools with their descriptions, argument schemas, and effects.\"},{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/v1/tools/authorize\",\"purpose\":\"Check whether a tool call is authorized without invoking it.\",\"body\":{\"required\":[\"name\"],\"optional\":[\"arguments\"]}},{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/v1/tools/call\",\"purpose\":\"Invoke a registered tool. Read GET /v1/tools first for the selected tool's argument schema.\",\"body\":{\"required\":[\"name\"],\"optional\":[\"arguments\"]}},{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/v1/runs\",\"purpose\":\"Create a durable run. Returns 202 for a new run and 200 for an idempotent replay.\",\"body\":{\"required\":[\"version=1\",\"command_id\",\"run_id\",\"provider\",\"model\"],\"optional\":[\"prompt\",\"execution_target=worker\",\"parent_run_id\",\"parent_agent_id\",\"conversation_id\",\"routing_profile\",\"workflow_id\",\"workflow_version=1\",\"node_id\",\"depends_on\",\"allow_external_dependencies\"]}},{\"method\":\"GET\",\"methods\":[\"GET\"],\"path\":\"/v1/runs/{run_id}\",\"purpose\":\"Return the projected durable state of a run, including status and terminal.\"},{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/v1/runs/{run_id}/cancel\",\"purpose\":\"Cancel a non-terminal run. The body run_id must match the path.\",\"body\":{\"required\":[\"version=1\",\"command_id\",\"run_id\"]}},{\"method\":\"GET\",\"methods\":[\"GET\"],\"path\":\"/v1/runs/{run_id}/events\",\"purpose\":\"Read durable events after an optional numeric ?after= cursor.\",\"response\":{\"fields\":[\"version\",\"run_id\",\"events\",\"next_cursor\"]}},{\"method\":\"GET\",\"methods\":[\"GET\"],\"path\":\"/v1/runs/{run_id}/events/stream\",\"purpose\":\"Stream new durable events as SSE and close at terminal state. Resume with ?after= or Last-Event-ID.\"},{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/v1/runs/{run_id}/assessments\",\"purpose\":\"Record an idempotent supervisor assessment. The body run_id must match the path.\",\"body\":{\"required\":[\"version=1\",\"command_id\",\"run_id\",\"verdict\"],\"optional\":[\"score\",\"rationale\"]}},{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/v1/runs/{run_id}/interventions\",\"purpose\":\"Request an idempotent supervisor intervention; currently action must be cancel.\",\"body\":{\"required\":[\"version=1\",\"command_id\",\"run_id\",\"action=cancel\"],\"optional\":[\"reason\"]}},{\"method\":\"GET\",\"methods\":[\"GET\"],\"path\":\"/v1/workflows/{workflow_id}\",\"purpose\":\"Return the durable workflow graph projected from its runs.\"},{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/v1/workers/register\",\"purpose\":\"Register an external worker before claiming runs.\",\"body\":{\"required\":[\"version=1\",\"worker_id\",\"capabilities.agent_process=true\"]}},{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/v1/workers/claim\",\"purpose\":\"Claim the next queued worker run. The command_id becomes the lease_id; an empty queue returns status empty.\",\"body\":{\"required\":[\"version=1\",\"command_id\",\"worker_id\"],\"optional\":[\"lease_ms; default 30000\"]}},{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/v1/workers/heartbeat\",\"purpose\":\"Renew the current unexpired lease.\",\"body\":{\"required\":[\"version=1\",\"command_id\",\"run_id\",\"worker_id\",\"lease_id\"],\"optional\":[\"lease_ms; default 30000\"]}},{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/v1/workers/progress\",\"purpose\":\"Append progress from the current lease holder.\",\"body\":{\"required\":[\"version=1\",\"command_id\",\"run_id\",\"worker_id\",\"lease_id\",\"event\"]}},{\"method\":\"POST\",\"methods\":[\"POST\"],\"path\":\"/v1/workers/complete\",\"purpose\":\"Finish the current leased run. outcome=succeeded completes it; any other outcome fails it.\",\"body\":{\"required\":[\"version=1\",\"run_id\",\"worker_id\",\"lease_id\",\"outcome\"],\"optional\":[\"output\",\"provider\",\"model\"]}}],\"worker_protocol\":[\"POST /v1/workers/register with agent_process=true\",\"POST /v1/workers/claim using a fresh command_id\",\"Execute the returned assignment while renewing the lease before lease_expires_at_ms\",\"POST progress events as useful\",\"POST complete before the lease expires\"]}")

;;; The default representation is deliberately written for an agent arriving
;;; with no other project context. Paths are rooted at /agents so examples can
;;; be copied directly from the URL that supplied this guide.
(defn harness-api-reference-text [] (-> (slice u8))
  "COIL AGENT HARNESS API v1\n\nThis service creates durable agent runs, exposes harness tools, and lets external workers execute queued runs. All examples below are relative to this origin and use the /agents route. Send JSON bodies with Content-Type: application/json.\n\nSTART HERE\n1. Discover the tools that are actually installed:\n   GET /agents/v1/tools\n2. Invoke one using the argument schema returned above:\n   POST /agents/v1/tools/call\n   {\"name\":\"echo\",\"arguments\":{\"text\":\"hello\"}}\n3. Create a durable run:\n   POST /agents/v1/runs\n   {\"version\":1,\"command_id\":\"create-unique-id\",\"run_id\":\"run-unique-id\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"prompt\":\"Inspect the workspace and report what you find.\"}\n4. Inspect it and follow its events:\n   GET /agents/v1/runs/{run_id}\n   GET /agents/v1/runs/{run_id}/events?after=0\n   GET /agents/v1/runs/{run_id}/events/stream?after=0\n\nRUNS\nPOST /agents/v1/runs requires version=1, unique command_id, unique run_id, provider, and model. prompt is optional. A new run returns 202; retrying the same command_id is idempotent and returns the existing run. Set execution_target to worker to queue it for an external worker instead of starting it in this process. Optional hierarchy/workflow fields are parent_run_id, parent_agent_id, conversation_id, routing_profile, workflow_id, workflow_version=1, node_id, depends_on, and allow_external_dependencies.\n\nGET /agents/v1/runs/{run_id} returns projected durable state. POST /agents/v1/runs/{run_id}/cancel takes {\"version\":1,\"command_id\":\"cancel-unique-id\",\"run_id\":\"the-same-path-id\"}.\n\nEVENTS\nThe polling endpoint returns version, run_id, events, and next_cursor. Resume with ?after=<next_cursor>. The SSE endpoint emits durable sequence values as id and event batches as data, accepts ?after=<sequence> or Last-Event-ID, sends keep-alives while idle, and closes after terminal state.\n\nWORKERS\nTo execute runs created with execution_target=worker:\n1. POST /agents/v1/workers/register\n   {\"version\":1,\"worker_id\":\"worker-unique-id\",\"capabilities\":{\"agent_process\":true}}\n2. POST /agents/v1/workers/claim\n   {\"version\":1,\"command_id\":\"lease-unique-id\",\"worker_id\":\"worker-unique-id\",\"lease_ms\":30000}\n   status=empty means there is no queued work. When claimed, command_id becomes lease_id and assignment contains the run request.\n3. Before lease_expires_at_ms, renew with POST /agents/v1/workers/heartbeat using version, a fresh command_id, run_id, worker_id, lease_id, and optional lease_ms.\n4. Report events with POST /agents/v1/workers/progress using version, a fresh command_id, run_id, worker_id, lease_id, and event.\n5. Finish with POST /agents/v1/workers/complete using version, run_id, worker_id, lease_id, outcome, and optional output. outcome=succeeded completes the run; other outcomes fail it.\n\nSUPERVISION AND WORKFLOWS\nPOST /agents/v1/runs/{run_id}/assessments requires version=1, command_id, matching run_id, and verdict; score and rationale are optional. POST /agents/v1/runs/{run_id}/interventions requires version=1, command_id, matching run_id, and action=cancel; reason is optional. GET /agents/v1/workflows/{workflow_id} returns the projected workflow graph.\n\nERRORS\nBuffered errors are JSON with error and message. Expect 400 for malformed commands, 404 for missing routes/resources, 409 for conflicts or invalid leases, 501 when no tool plane exists, and 500/503 for persistence or startup failures. Reuse command_id only when retrying the same intended mutation.\n\nMACHINE-READABLE GUIDE\nGET /agents?format=json or send Accept: application/json.\n")

;;; This is the product guide. A workflow means the Markdown-defined software
;;; factory throughout this document; the durable-run HTTP protocol is an
;;; implementation surface and deliberately comes last.
(defn harness-api-description-text [] (-> (slice u8))
  "COIL SOFTWARE FACTORY\n\nThe main job of this harness is to run reusable Markdown-defined workflows against named projects. Start with projects and workflow files. Do not start by constructing low-level /v1/runs requests.\n\n1. DECLARE THE PROJECT\n\nA project is a stable name for an existing checkout. Declare it once in $HARNESS_CONFIG_DIR/projects.json (normally ~/.coil-agent-harness/projects.json):\n\n  {\n    \"version\": 1,\n    \"projects\": [\n      {\"name\":\"my-repo\",\"path\":\"/absolute/path/to/repo\",\"label\":\"My repo\",\"summary\":\"What this codebase is\"}\n    ]\n  }\n\nList and validate what the harness sees:\n\n  harness projects\n\nNever point a workflow at an undeclared name and never work directly in the checkout. The harness creates an isolated Git worktree and branch for each run and commits worker results there.\n\n2. CREATE A MARKDOWN WORKFLOW\n\nA workflow is a reusable directory, conventionally under factories/. Scaffold one or several ordered workers:\n\n  harness factory new factories/review implement verify\n\nThat creates factory.json, context.md, and ordered worker Markdown files such as 01-implement.md and 02-verify.md. Edit those files; the Markdown is the actual worker assignment. A minimal definition is:\n\n  factories/review/factory.json\n  {\n    \"name\": \"review\",\n    \"goal\": \"Implement the requested change and prove it works.\",\n    \"context\": [\"context.md\"],\n    \"tools\": {\"groups\": [\"filesystem\", \"bash\"]},\n    \"commands\": {\"before\": [], \"after\": [], \"before_each\": [], \"after_each\": []},\n    \"workers\": [\"01-implement.md\", \"02-verify.md\"]\n  }\n\n  factories/review/context.md\n  # Shared context\n  State invariants, constraints, acceptance criteria, and facts every worker needs.\n\n  factories/review/01-implement.md\n  # Implement\n  Inspect the project, implement the requested change, run relevant checks, and report concrete evidence.\n\n  factories/review/02-verify.md\n  # Verify\n  Review the implementation independently, run the project tests, and fix failures before declaring it ready.\n\nKeep reusable process in worker Markdown and shared invariants in context.md. A workflow belongs to no project; choose the project only when starting a run.\n\n3. RUN THE WORKFLOW ON A PROJECT\n\n  harness factory run factories/review --project my-repo\n\nChoose a model or provider only when the workflow needs a non-default one:\n\n  harness factory run factories/review --project my-repo --provider codex --model gpt-5.6-terra\n\nFor a workflow whose factory.json declares an input such as issue, give it a Markdown issue file instead:\n\n  harness factory issue factories/issues --issue .factory-issues/change.md --project my-repo\n\nThe command prints four important facts: factory workspace, factory branch, factory journal, and the snapshotted factory definition. Preserve those. Review or merge the resulting branch; do not copy changes out of the original checkout by hand.\n\n4. WATCH AND STEER THE RUN\n\nThe journal under .factory-runs/<workflow>/<timestamp>.jsonl is the durable record. Workers can inspect the live Markdown topology with inspect_workflow and route with set_workflow_state. Each worker must call report_worker_status with ready, summary, and evidence. Use the printed run identity with the harness status/watch/TUI commands, and send a focused correction with harness say <run-id> <message> when a live worker needs direction.\n\n5. DESIGN RULES\n\n- Project = a named checkout. Workflow = reusable Markdown instructions. Run = one execution of that workflow in an isolated worktree. Do not collapse these nouns.\n- Put the desired outcome in goal, stable facts in context Markdown, and role-specific work in ordered worker Markdown.\n- Verification is a real worker or command gate, not a sentence asking the implementer to be careful.\n- before/after and before_each/after_each commands are deterministic lifecycle gates; they stop on the first nonzero exit.\n- Workflows that need an issue must be started with factory issue and a real Markdown issue file.\n- A failed worktree isolation stops the run. The harness never falls back to modifying the project checkout.\n\nADVANCED: NATIVE SERVICE PROTOCOL\n\nThe authenticated /agents/v1/* endpoints expose tools, individual durable runs, event polling/SSE, supervision, workflow DAG projection, and the external-worker lease protocol. They are infrastructure for integrations; they are not the normal way to create and run a Markdown software factory. Fetch /agents?format=json for their complete machine-readable schemas and examples.\n")
